    "summary": "Epic impact: covers Story s1 -- s1 built and landed sc1/sc2 matching their HLD interfaceSketches exactly. This Task replaces startTurn's mode:'read-only' placeholder throw with real dispatch: re-check the qualification cache fresh by stableDescriptorHash at dispatch time (never trusting readOnly's construction-time snapshot, matching the LLD's own edge-case wording that the cache is \"always re-checked... at dispatch time\"), dispatch via runTurn (s1's own real-dispatch path, reused unchanged -- buildArgv's read-only branch from t2 applies automatically since request.mode is 'read-only'), throw VibeReadOnlyUnavailableError with the cached reason before any process spawns when unavailable. The post-dispatch fingerprint check wraps runTurn's own injectable `rm` cleanup seam (reading export.json's fingerprint before the real cleanup deletes it) rather than modifying runTurn or any s1-owned type, since rm runs in runTurn's own finally AFTER resolveResult/rejectResult already settled -- the mismatch invalidates the cache for the NEXT call only, never the current call's own already-returned result. Left out: nothing from this Task's scope; t4's deferred trigger-on-miss (disclosed in t4's own build record) is NOT addressed here either -- it still requires a design decision about who proactively re-qualifies a cold descriptor, which this Task's own scope (dispatch-time recheck of an EXISTING cache entry) does not cover.",
